From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:31:42 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-vb

Nintendo Virtual Boy gets one shelf, Games/VB, on Beetle VB
(mednafen_vb) alone. Platform::Vb is appended to SHELVES and
Core::MednafenVb to EVERY; upstream's ALL lists stay as they are. Carts
are .vb and .vboy, titled by their stem (the header title is often
Japanese). Every policy method answers Virtual Boy explicitly: L and R go
to the game, X and Y reach slot's input map (patch vb-input), L2 and R2
stay slot's rewind and fast-forward, Select+X flips the picture, no core
picker, no crop, rewind on. The 384x224 picture sits on a 384x256 canvas,
3:2 like the panel, so it scales 1.875x to 720x420 with Actual (the
default) and fills 720x480 with Stretch. Its shader is stored in
Config/vb_shader.txt and offers the retro list. Saves/VB, States/VB and
Labels/VB are made at boot. The shelf shows the SNES cart until the
Virtual Boy cart lands.
